  "summary_en": "Singapore bill amending the Active Mobility Act, Electric Vehicles Charging Act, Road Traffic Act and Small Motorised Vehicles (Safety) Act. Among its provisions, it creates a regulatory framework for autonomous motor vehicle trials, special uses and testbeds on public paths. It also tightens rules on sale and advertising of personal mobility devices and batteries, and on EV chargers.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "New Division 2C of Active Mobility Act regulates autonomous motor vehicle trials, special uses and testbeds on public paths via ministerial regulations",
   "Authorised persons must hold liability insurance, publish notices, keep sensor data and video records, and maintain vehicle and operator registers",
   "Regulations may exempt or modify Road Traffic Act and AMA provisions; the framework sunsets 30 September 2031",
   "Road Traffic Act sandbox sunset for autonomous vehicles extended to 31 December 2028",
   "New offences for interfering with approved AV trials and for selling or altering unsafe PABs/PMDs; LTA gets directions power over online marketplaces"
